  "_note_konjunktiv": "German B2's Konjunktiv (course-de-b2-a). nonstandard, after a verb of saying (not after ich, whose form these are): the present and the Konjunktiv II that talk has for a reported Konjunktiv I (Er sagt, er ist krank; er wäre krank; sie kommen for sie kämen); after als ob, als wenn, wie wenn: the present for the Konjunktiv II (als ob er krank ist). One rule a word, since a rule can't tie one verb's two forms together. wrong: worden against wurden and werden; soll against will in all their forms; a long participle without its ge; geöffnet against eröffnet; seinen against seien.",
  "_b2c_note": "German B2's text and register (course-de-b2-c). same: so dass is sodass, in Frage is infrage, anderseits and andrerseits are andererseits (Duden has each). wrong, a word of its own and no slip: war for zwar; teuer, neuer, Feuer and heuer, Fieber and Feber, Pause and Jause, Tropfen and Topfen, Kessel and Sessel, Kosten, Karten, Kisten and Kasten, Männer and Jänner; biete and bitte, versuche and ersuche; stehle for stelle, sehe for stehe; lasse, passe for fasse. A German-German word beside an Austrian one is an accept, never a rule here."
